530:A crucial contribution to the theory of sharp thresholds is due to Friedgut, in the form of a general existence theorem for sharp thresholds (see \cite{Friedgut05}, \cite{FrBo99}). Roughly, the theorem asserts that if a monotone symmetric property has a coarse threshold, then it can be approximated by the property of containing a small fixed subgraph.
