## Gate results

| Gate | Result | Measurement |
|---|---|---|
| G1 | pass | 12/12 preset-seed plants verify and JSON round-trip; compact solver independently succeeds |
| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
| G3 | pass | tagged prose and fenced JSON round-trip; garbage returns `None` |
| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; exact density `2^-83` |
| G5 | pass | one certified shipping solution; demo brute-force count 1; reference cost measured |
| G6 | pass | four attacks each 0/8; Gaussian elimination 8/8 as expected |
| G7 | pass | doubled `n=166`, `m=1,366` instance builds and verifies |
| G8 | pass | 80/80 symmetry and carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
| G9(c) | pass | 280 characters, 70 estimated tokens, 83 atoms, 248 exact XORs |
| G9(a,b) | **not run** | OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 key-limit errors for every vendor redraw |

The four failing attacks are occurrence-degree parity, four-pass single-bit
coordinate descent, 256 uniform random restarts, and a left-to-right zero-fill
completion heuristic.  The last is an executable in-context strategy rather
than a disguised solver.  The successful standard algorithm is reported only
under `reference_algorithm`, as Track B requires.

