/tmp/arxiv1504.DMSE1R/src/planted_random15_4.tex:245:%We also look at a family of CSPs which are related to a candidate one-way function proposed by Goldreich which has received some attention in the cryptography literature (cite some references).
/tmp/arxiv1504.DMSE1R/src/planted_random15_4.tex:248:%We are motivated in particular by the work of the first author and Montanari who studied the threshold behaviour of the number of solutions of random (not planted) $k$-SAT formulae.
