   371	\begin{theorem}\label{thm:main}
   372	For every $k\geq 2$, there exist a countable set $\mathcal D$ and a function $\phi_s: [0,\alpha^*] \to [0,1]$ such that for every $\alpha \notin \mathcal D$ and every $\epsilon > 0$,
   373	$$\lim_{n\to \infty} Q_n(\alpha, \phi_s(\alpha)-\epsilon) = 0 $$
